    "function": "Involved in the biosynthesis of polyacyltrehalose (PAT), a pentaacylated, trehalose-based glycolipid that could have a role in anchoring the bacterial capsule. Catalyzes the sequential transfer of two palmitoyl groups onto a single glucose residue of trehalose generating the diacylated product 2,3-diacyltrehalose (trehalose dipalmitate). Although palmitoyl-CoA (PCoA) seems to be the physiological acyl donor, PapA3 can also use docosanoyl (22-carbon saturated fatty acid) coenzyme A as acyl donor",
